{"title":"Check If The Number Is Fascinating","difficulty":"Easy","statement":"You are given an integer n that consists of exactly 3 digits.\nWe call the number n fascinating if, after the following modification, the resulting number contains all the digits from 1 to 9 exactly once and does not contain any 0's:\n\nConcatenate n with the numbers 2 * n and 3 * n.\n\nReturn true if n is fascinating, or false otherwise.\nConcatenating two numbers means joining them together. For example, the concatenation of 121 and 371 is 121371.\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n```text\nInput: n = 192\nOutput: true\n```\nExplanation: We concatenate the numbers n = 192 and 2 * n = 384 and 3 * n = 576. The resulting number is 192384576. This number contains all the digits from 1 to 9 exactly once.\n### Example 2\n```text\nInput: n = 100\nOutput: false\n```\nExplanation: We concatenate the numbers n = 100 and 2 * n = 200 and 3 * n = 300. The resulting number is 100200300. This number does not satisfy any of the conditions.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 100 <= n <= 999\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def isFascinating(self, n: int) -> bool:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().isFascinating","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"}],"returnType":"bool","tests":[{"input":[100],"expected":false},{"input":[101],"expected":false},{"input":[102],"expected":false},{"input":[104],"expected":false},{"input":[105],"expected":false},{"input":[107],"expected":false},{"input":[110],"expected":false},{"input":[111],"expected":false},{"input":[112],"expected":false},{"input":[114],"expected":false},{"input":[115],"expected":false},{"input":[116],"expected":false},{"input":[117],"expected":false},{"input":[118],"expected":false},{"input":[120],"expected":false},{"input":[124],"expected":false},{"input":[125],"expected":false},{"input":[126],"expected":false},{"input":[127],"expected":false},{"input":[129],"expected":false},{"input":[130],"expected":false},{"input":[132],"expected":false},{"input":[134